{"nodes": [{"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation", "label": "Phase 1 \u2014 Multi-Tenant Foundation (v2.0 milestone)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "1-542", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_supabase_over_neon", "label": "Supabase Postgres over Neon", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "36-46", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "RLS policies need auth.uid(); with Supabase, Auth and Postgres are one vendor so policies read the verified JWT natively with zero cross-vendor plumbing and isolation genuinely lives in the DB. Neon's stateless HTTP driver also cannot hold the per-session/per-transaction variable RLS leans on, which would push isolation back up into app code \u2014 exactly what PITFALLS #8 warns against."}, {"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_email_phone_split", "label": "Split contact into email + phone in the DB", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "122-127", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lead.contact is a single polymorphic, unvalidated string (email OR phone). You cannot reliably dedupe on that, and dedupe is load-bearing: PITFALLS #11's double-counted revenue is a correctness bug in the product's headline number. The TS Lead type keeps contact unchanged (all baseLead factories depend on it); the hydrator sets contact = email ?? phone \u2014 a mapping layer, not a breaking change."}, {"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_lead_identities_own_table", "label": "Identities get their own table", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "129-133", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A lead can be reachable by both an email and a phone, and the same human can arrive twice through different pipes. A one-column dedupe key cannot model that. lead_identities lets an incoming lead match on ANY identity and merge onto the existing row."}, {"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_two_dedupe_keys", "label": "Two dedupe keys, precisely", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "228-243", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two different problems need two different keys. Duplicate POST (Typeform retry, Calendly redelivery) \u2192 dedupe_key = sha256(source_id + (provider_event_id ?? canonical_json(payload))) under unique(customer_id, dedupe_key) on lead_events. Same human via form AND email \u2192 normalized identity under unique(customer_id, kind, value_normalized) on lead_identities. One key cannot do both: idempotency is per-delivery, identity is per-person. Ingest resolves normalize \u2192 look up lead_identities \u2192 hit merges, miss inserts lead + identity. Upsert, never blind insert (PITFALLS #2)."}, {"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_webhook_hole", "label": "The webhook isolation hole", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "280-311", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Webhook ingest is unauthenticated by design \u2014 a form tool POSTs to a secret URL, so there is no user JWT, auth.uid() is null, and every authenticated-role policy evaluates false. This is the single biggest isolation risk in the whole design."}, {"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_ingest_role", "label": "ingest_role scoped by transaction-local app.customer_id", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "284-303", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A dedicated role that is deliberately NOT BYPASSRLS. Each ingest write runs in a transaction that does `set local app.customer_id = '<resolved-from-webhook-token>'`, with policies keyed on current_setting('app.customer_id', true)::uuid for both using and with check. A bug in the ingest handler then cannot write across tenants \u2014 the DB refuses. Requires a transaction-capable connection (Supavisor transaction mode + postgres.js), not a stateless HTTP driver \u2014 a second reason Supabase beat Neon."}, {"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_service_role_fallback", "label": "service_role fallback for ingest (rejected alternative)", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "305-311", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Only if the pooler fights the GUC: service_role bypasses RLS entirely, reachable through a single auditable repository module (packages/db/src/repo/ingest.ts) taking customerId as every function's first argument. Tradeoff stated plainly \u2014 it moves isolation from the DB back into app code for the ingest path. The service-role key must never reach the client: server-only, unprefixed."}, {"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_current_customer_id", "label": "public.current_customer_id() helper function", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "254-260", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "security definer, stable, search_path = public; selects customers.id where auth_user_id = (select auth.uid()) so the customer lookup is written once instead of per policy."}, {"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_tenant_isolation_policy", "label": "tenant_isolation policy shape", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "262-273", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Repeated per tenant table: for all to authenticated, using and with check both customer_id = (select public.current_customer_id()). RLS is enabled in the same migration that creates the table, plus force row level security so even the table owner is subject to policy."}, {"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_select_wrapping", "label": "(select ...) InitPlan wrapping in policies", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "271-276", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Wrapping in (select ...) lets Postgres cache the value as an InitPlan instead of re-evaluating it per row. Flagged for verification against the Supabase RLS performance best-practices page."}, {"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_isolation_test", "label": "Cross-tenant isolation test (phase acceptance gate)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "314-338", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "vitest at packages/db/src/__tests__/tenant-isolation.test.ts against a local Supabase. Seeds customer A (3 leads) and B (2 leads) from real supabase.auth.signUp() sessions and asserts: correct row counts per tenant, B's lead id returns 0 rows (empty not error), insert with the other tenant's customer_id is rejected by with check, cross-tenant update affects 0 rows, repeated for lead_events, lead_identities, detection_settings, push_tokens, and that the ingest path with A's webhook token cannot write B's customer_id."}, {"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_negative_control", "label": "Negative control \u2014 a green test that cannot fail is worse than no test", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "488-510", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Step 7's second half matters as much as the first: flipping one policy to using (true) must make the isolation suite FAIL. Confirm RED, then revert. A green isolation test that cannot fail is worse than no test."}, {"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_anon_key_client", "label": "Use the anon key, never service_role, for isolation assertions", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "330-334", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Two real sessions via supabase.auth.signUp(), then createClient(url, ANON_KEY, { global: { headers: { Authorization: 'Bearer ' + jwt }}}) per tenant. A service-role client bypasses RLS and would make the test pass while proving nothing \u2014 noted in a comment because it is the easiest way for this test to silently rot."}, {"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_pglite_not_substitute", "label": "pglite is not a substitute for Docker Supabase", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "336-339", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "pglite has no GoTrue/auth schema, so auth.uid() does not exist and the policies under test cannot even be created. Docker is required. Flagged as unverified."}, {"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_resolve_customer", "label": "resolveCustomer \u2014 session \u2192 customer_id resolver", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "342-368", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "api/_lib/auth.ts returns Resolved { ok: true, userId, customerId, jwt } or AuthFailure { ok: false, status: 401|403, code }. Failure modes explicit, never silent: missing/malformed header \u2192 401; valid JWT but no customers row \u2192 403 no_customer, never an auto-create, because silently minting tenants on a stray token is how cross-tenant bugs start."}, {"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_get_claims", "label": "supabase.auth.getClaims() for JWT verification", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "359-364", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Preferred over getUser(): getClaims verifies the JWT against the cached JWKS endpoint /.well-known/jwks.json instead of always round-tripping to the Auth server, removing one network hop per request. jose + cached JWKS is the manual equivalent."}, {"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_normalization_rules", "label": "Email/phone normalization rules", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "234-239", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Pure and unit-tested in packages/core. email \u2192 trim().toLowerCase() and nothing cleverer: no gmail dot-stripping or plus-tag removal, because that over-merges distinct people and is unrecoverable once merged. phone \u2192 strip non-digits, drop a leading 1 if 11 digits, keep the last 10 (NANP-shaped, fits the local-service-business target); the original stays untouched in phone."}, {"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_lead_statuses_constants", "label": "LEAD_STATUSES as single source of truth", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "403-417", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The status list was hardcoded in four places and had already diverged (revenue.ts:23 counts booked as recovered while leaks.ts:21 treats it as merely terminal). Export LEAD_STATUSES / TERMINAL_STATUSES / RECOVERED_STATUSES and generate pgEnum('lead_status', LEAD_STATUSES) rather than retyping it. Keep the booked-is-recovered behaviour \u2014 a product question, not a Phase 1 refactor \u2014 but make it named instead of accidental."}, {"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_parser_date_bug", "label": "Parser date-field bug (last_contact_at / next_follow_up_at)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "374-381", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Both fields are in HEADER_MAP but never written into the pushed object, so every CSV lead looks no_reply and slow_reply / no_follow_up / stale_quote are unreachable \u2014 half the engine is dead, and the DB would faithfully persist nulls the parser can never fill. Fixed TDD: failing test in parser.test.ts first."}, {"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_detection_config", "label": "DetectionConfig \u2014 parameterized leak thresholds", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "383-402", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "detectLeaks gains a third positional arg defaulting to DEFAULT_DETECTION_CONFIG { slowReplyHours: 24, staleQuoteDays: 7 }, so both existing call sites and every test keep working untouched \u2014 and detection_settings has something to bind to."}, {"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_estimated_value_cents", "label": "estimated_value stored as integer cents", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "169-179", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Integer cents throughout \u2014 a float column here silently corrupts money. The surrogate uuid id also replaces the positional `row-${i}` lead_id fallback, which collides across two imports of different files."}, {"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_auth_user_id_column", "label": "auth_user_id as a separate column from customers.id", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "142-144", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Solo-owner today (team roles are an anti-feature), but keeping auth_user_id separate stops many-users-per-customer from requiring a migration of every FK later. Cheap insurance."}, {"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_database_url_direct", "label": "DATABASE_URL_DIRECT vs pooled DATABASE_URL", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "460-473", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Functions use the Supavisor transaction pooler; drizzle-kit migrations use the direct/session connection because poolers in transaction mode reject the session state DDL needs. SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY is server-only and never client-exposed; VITE_/EXPO_PUBLIC_ anon keys are public by design."}, {"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_greedy_spa_rewrite", "label": "Greedy SPA rewrite in vercel.json", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "444-454", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "{\"source\":\"/(.*)\"} is maximally greedy; Vercel normally matches api/ functions before rewrites but that precedence is not worth relying on. Change to the negative lookahead /((?!api/).*) and verify with a real request."}, {"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_esm_type_module", "label": "ESM / \"type\": \"module\" packaging trap", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "432-442", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "packages/core emits ESM but its exports.require points at the same ESM file, so a Vercel Node function doing require('@missed-lead/core') fails. Add \"type\":\"module\" to core and db and drop the false require conditions. Separately, vite aliases @missed-lead/core to dist, so the root build must compile workspaces first or core edits stay invisible."}, {"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_packages_db", "label": "packages/db (@missed-lead/db) workspace package", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "116-118", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Schema, migrations, and repository functions kept out of packages/core so core stays a pure, dependency-free engine."}, {"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_pitfalls", "label": ".planning/research/PITFALLS.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "19", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_architecture", "label": ".planning/research/ARCHITECTURE.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "15-16", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_product_direction_auto_capture", "label": ".planning/notes/product-direction-auto-capture.md", "file_type": "document", "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "6", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation", "target": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_supabase_over_neon", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "36-46", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation", "target": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_email_phone_split", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "122-127", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation", "target": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_lead_identities_own_table", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "129-133", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation", "target": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_two_dedupe_keys", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "228-243", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation", "target": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_webhook_hole", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "280-283", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation", "target": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_isolation_test", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "314-338", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation", "target": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_resolve_customer", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "342-368", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation", "target": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_parser_date_bug", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "374-381", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation", "target": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_detection_config", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "383-402", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation", "target": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_lead_statuses_constants", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "403-417", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation", "target": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_normalization_rules", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "234-239", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation", "target": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_packages_db", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "116-118", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation", "target": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_database_url_direct", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "460-473", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation", "target": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_greedy_spa_rewrite", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": ".planning/phases/phase-1-foundation.md", "source_location": "444-454", "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation", "target": "planning_phases_phase_1_foundation_esm_type_module", "relation": "references",